                                "sense_id": "71ab3bbb-004a-35c6-8a0b-833f0ee1176f",
                                "text": "1899, Mary A. Ward, Life and works of the sisters Brontë, Introduction to Jane Eyre\nAnd there can be no doubt that there was in Miss Bronte a curious vein of recklessness, roughness, one might also say - hoydenism - that exists side by side with an exquisite delicacy and a true dignity, and is none the less Irish and Celtic for that."
                            },
